<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day t-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day t-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 8.830 percent at Monday's auction from 8.958 percent at the previous auction on June 23.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 894.950 million pounds, are the first 182-day bills issued since a batch worth 800.500 million pounds matured on July 1. The treasury had asked for 800 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Jan 6, 1998 (Dec 23, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.830 percent (8.958)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 894.950 million (1,411.625 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,266.125 million (1,907.625 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.574-8.889 percent (8.600-9.048)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.574-10.200 percent (8.600-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 65 (88)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 104 (98)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
</text>
